*** ch13-13-comm-id — unification modulo commutativity + identity (CU): duplicated unifier in unify, minimal via irredundant unify (Maude manual §13.4.5)

mod COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EX is
 sorts Magma Elem .
 subsorts Elem < Magma .
 op __ : Magma Magma -> Magma [gather (E e) comm id: e] .
 ops a b c d e : -> Elem .
endm

unify in COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EX : X:Magma a =? Y:Magma a a .

irredundant unify in COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EX :
      X:Magma a =? Y:Magma a a .

*** manual writes "in COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EXAMPLE" here (typo); module is COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EX
unify in COMM-ID-UNIFICATION-EX : a X:Magma =? a a Y:Magma .
